## adding-forces

adding-forces-ask = What is the resultant of the two dynamometers’ forces?
adding-forces-title = Adding forces: the resultant
adding-forces-question = A { $mass } load hangs on a wooden ruler. We hold this load by one dynamometer, then by two at the ruler’s ends — the weights in the middle and nearer an end — and then one dynamometer pulls up and the other down. Each time we write down the readings. What is the resultant of the two dynamometers’ forces?
adding-forces-choices = Each time the same force as one dynamometer showed
adding-forces-choices-2 = More: there are two dynamometers
adding-forces-choices-3 = Less: each pulls weaker
adding-forces-setup = A stand, two dynamometers (up to 5 N), a wooden ruler, weights
adding-forces-mass = Mass of the load
adding-forces-optional = What if the weights are moved? Set their distance from the ruler’s middle in the field beside them, or drag them along the ruler.
